      "data": {
        "text": "SHIPPED -- PR #330 (merge into main), branch fix/ai-pingpong-seek deleted.\n\nRoot cause: the seek deadzone assumed a ship entering it COASTS, but the 90ms low-pass keeps Move() (magnitude discarded = full thrust) on the stale seek residual for ~125ms after the pull cuts -- ~41px through a 15px deadzone -- so every arrival orbited the station 0.5-2 loops (isolation sim of the exact pipeline).\n\nFix: velocity-aware cutoff (deadzone + speed * DefaultSeekArriveLeadMs 125, derived = SteerSmoothMs*ln(SeekWeight/NoiseFloor)), applied only after DefaultSeekArriveCalmMs 1500ms of zero threat pressure. Both eager variants were built and MEASURED WORSE (CrazyGame deaths 2.62 -> 6.00 / 5.25, ai_sweep seeds 1-8 x2) -- the orbit was incidental evasion in combat lulls, and a converging bullet shell cancels to sub-floor repulsion so nothing wakes a parked ship. The 1500ms hold covers the pre-card orbit's own settle time (1333ms), so combat is pre-card by construction: crazygame/spacedodge seed-for-seed IDENTICAL to ?aiseeklead=0, idle% flat.\n\nFiles: PlayerShip.cs (cutoff, threatPressure, aiCalmMs), DebugFlags.cs (?aiseeklead= ?aiseekcalm=), AiBench.cs (calm= / seeklead= observables), logic_probe ProbeAiSeekArrive + 2 rejection rows, probes ai_seek_arrive{,_absent}.txt, CLAUDE.md docs.\n\nMeasured at N=16/arm-rig (seeds 1-8 x2) -- the N=60 gate is the scoring pass's. Closed-loop jitter at a stationary destination: 2.01 loops -> 0.06 (probe-pinned). Live: Tutorial calm=84 seeklead=82; CrazyGame calm=0.",
